@* HelpGettingStartedPage: help topic "Getting started" at "/help/getting-started". Static text. *@
@page "/help/getting-started"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="getting-started">
    <section class="card">
        <ol>
            <li>Sign in with the user name and password an administrator gave you. After several failed attempts
                you are asked to wait a few minutes before you try again.</li>
            <li>Open <a href="/projects" data-testid="help-projects-link">Projects</a> and choose a project. You see
                only the projects you are a member of; if the list is empty, ask an administrator to add you. A
                system administrator creates projects (<strong>+ New project</strong>) and adds the members. A project
                groups the reviews of one body of work.</li>
            <li>On the project page, create a review: choose the files to review, give the review an identifier and a
                title, and create it. The review page opens, and its top line says what to do next.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="muted">Not sure where to go? The home page lists the main pages, and the menu bar is on every page.</p>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
